{"type":"ring","title":"Deeper buffers: deadlock later (4-chip ring)","intro":"A link carries data as <b>flits</b>, small fixed-size pieces of a packet (4 flits per packet here). The receiving chip keeps a buffer per link. A packet's first flit, its <b>head</b>, can enter a buffer once the previous packet's last flit has arrived there, so packets queue one behind another and their flits never mix. Here 4 chips form a ring and send clockwise, one flit per link per cycle; each link takes turns between traffic passing through and the chip's own packets. <br><br>Would deeper buffers help? Here every buffer holds 8 flits instead of 4, and the same burst is sent. The buffers absorb more of it and more packets arrive, but once every buffer is full the same loop of waits closes. Storage only postpones a deadlock. Preventing it takes routing whose dependencies cannot form a loop (Dally and Seitz, 1987), which is what virtual channels provide.","n":4,"vcs":1,"cap":8,"plen":4,"dateline":false,"packets":[[0,1],[2,0],[1,3],[3,1],[0,2],[2,3],[0,3],[1,0],[0,3],[0,3],[1,3],[2,1],[2,1],[3,1],[1,0],[3,2],[2,0],[3,2]],"frames":[{"b":[[],[],[],[]],"q":[[[0,0]],[],[],[]],"w":[],"d":0},{"b":[[],[[0,0]],[],[]],"q":[[[0,1]],[],[[1,0]],[]],"w":[],"d":0},{"b":[[],[[0,1]],[],[[1,0]]],"q":[[[0,2]],[],[[1,1]],[]],"w":[],"d":0},{"b":[[[1,0]],[[0,2]],[],[[1,1]]],"q":[[[0,3]],[[2,0]],[[1,2]],[]],"w":[],"d":0},{"b":[[[1,1]],[[0,3]],[[2,0]],[[1,2]]],"q":[[],[[2,1]],[[1,3]],[]],"w":[[2,0,3,0]],"d":0},{"b":[[[1,2]],[],[[2,0],[2,1]],[[1,3]]],"q":[[],[[2,2]],[],[[3,0]]],"w":[],"d":1},{"b":[[[1,3]],[],[[2,1],[2,2]],[[2,0]]],"q":[[],[[2,3]],[],[[3,0]]],"w":[],"d":1},{"b":[[[3,0]],[],[[2,2],[2,3]],[[2,1]]],"q":[[],[],[],[[3,1]]],"w":[],"d":2},{"b":[[[3,1]],[[3,0]],[[2,3]],[[2,2]]],"q":[[[4,0]],[],[],[[3,2]]],"w":[],"d":2},{"b":[[[3,2]],[[3,1]],[],[[2,3]]],"q":[[[4,0]],[],[[5,0]],[[3,3]]],"w":[],"d":2},{"b":[[[3,3]],[[3,2]],[],[[5,0]]],"q":[[[4,0]],[],[[5,1]],[]],"w":[],"d":3},{"b":[[],[[3,3]],[],[[5,1]]],"